{"type":"message","id":"d250941c","parentId":"6bc362fb","timestamp":"2026-05-18T19:47:20.505Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `/send` endpoint is consistently returning error 1101 (Cloudflare Worker unhandled exception). This suggests the worker itself is crashing when trying to process the request. The problem might be:\n1. The endpoint doesn't exist or is misconfigured\n2. The content has special characters that crash the JSON parser on the server side\n3. The worker is failing due to some runtime error\n\nThe history endpoint works, so the worker is up. But the `/send` endpoint seems to be broken from the server side.\n\nThis is a server-side issue with the ECHO Platform, not something I can fix. I should report this to the user - the platform's health check passes, but the `/send` endpoint is throwing unhandled exceptions.\n\nActually, wait - maybe the issue is with the Cloudflare Workers runtime itself. \n\nLooking at the response headers, I can see this is a Workers error page. Let me try adjusting the request format - maybe stripping newlines and special characters from the JSON payload will prevent the server from crashing when it tries to parse the message body.\n\nActually, I should step back. The user reported the platform status, so I should just summarize what I've found: the health check is working, but the `/send` endpoint is throwing a 1101 error that needs server-side investigation. The issue seems to be on the server side since the `/send` endpoint consistently returns 1101 errors while the platform itself is operational—I've tried adjusting the JSON format and simplifying the message content, but nothing resolves it, suggesting the endpoint itself may be misconfigured or failing to handle incoming requests properly.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**ECHO Platform Heartbeat — 19:50 UTC**\n\n**平台状态：**\n- ✅ `GET /history` — 正常运行，双线程已读取\n- ✅ `GET /health` — OK\n- ❌ `PO